from the chief priests and the scribes and the elders.

82
00:05:31,980 --> 00:05:34,600
Now the betrayer had given them a sign, saying,

83
00:05:34,980 --> 00:05:36,680
The one I will kiss is the man.

84
00:05:36,680 --> 00:05:38,520
Seize him and lead him away under guard.

85
00:05:39,080 --> 00:05:42,840
And when he came, he went up to him at once and said,

86
00:05:43,420 --> 00:05:43,980
Rabbi.

87
00:05:45,180 --> 00:05:46,240
And he kissed him.

88
00:05:46,700 --> 00:05:48,800
And they laid hands on him and seized him.

89
00:05:49,240 --> 00:05:51,600
But one of those who stood by drew his sword

90
00:05:51,600 --> 00:05:53,300
and struck the servant of the high priest

91
00:05:53,300 --> 00:05:54,380
and cut off his ear.

92
00:05:54,800 --> 00:05:56,120
And Jesus said to them,

93
00:05:56,660 --> 00:05:58,880
Have you come out as against a robber

94
00:05:58,880 --> 00:06:01,020
with swords and clubs to capture me?

95
00:06:01,640 --> 00:06:04,080
Day after day I was with you in the temple teaching,

96
00:06:04,080 --> 00:06:05,700
and you did not seize me.

97
00:06:06,460 --> 00:06:08,360
But let the scriptures be fulfilled.

98
00:06:08,920 --> 00:06:11,020
And they all left him and fled.

99
00:06:11,900 --> 00:06:13,220
And a young man followed him

100
00:06:13,220 --> 00:06:15,460
with nothing but a linen cloth about his body.

101
00:06:15,860 --> 00:06:16,920
And they seized him,

102
00:06:17,220 --> 00:06:19,640
but he left the linen cloth and ran away naked.

103
00:06:20,900 --> 00:06:23,080
And they led Jesus to the high priest,

104
00:06:23,340 --> 00:06:25,280
and all the chief priests and the elders

105
